{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetRbgTQbVWRAPbZrF9RH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear understanding. Let me compile my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11` - Order entity currently has no status field\n- `OrderController.kt:15-46` - Contains POST create, GET, and list endpoints; needs cancel endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt:10-27` - In-memory store with save, existsById, findById, findAll methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` - Creates shipments without checking order status\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` - In-memory store needs a method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ApiException.kt:11-30` - ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) already exist\n- `ErrorCode.kt:31-37` - Has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS; needs new codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28` - Centralized exception handling\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw exceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError responses with status codes\n2. Tests use MockMvc and assert both status AND response body shape (error envelope)\n3. Tests verify state persistence with separate GET requests after mutations\n4. Tests assert error codes (not just status) for at least one failure case\n5. No service layer; logic in controllers\n6. In-memory repositories without transactions require explicit all-or-nothing logic\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - Add OrderStatus enum and status field (required for state tracking)\n2. `OrderController.kt` - Add POST cancel endpoint (required for feature)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Add findByOrderId() method (required to find shipments for cancellation)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` - Check order status on shipment creation (required by constraint)\n5. `ApiError.kt` - Add error codes for cancel rejection scenarios (required for error responses)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - Add cancel endpoint tests (required for acceptance criteria)\n\n**Risks:**\n- The in-memory store has no transactions; the cancel must atomically check and update both orders and shipments without a database transaction\n- Idempotency requires that re-cancelling an already-CANCELLED order must succeed and return the order\n- All-or-nothing means if any shipment is CONFIRMED, the entire cancel fails with nothing changed\n- Shipment creation must be able to look up order status\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone identified. The ticket is clear on semantics and error codes.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - for when trying to create a shipment on a cancelled order\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL` - for when cancel is rejected due to a confirmed shipment (or use existing CONFLICT status with descriptive message)\n\n2. **Order.kt** - Add `OrderStatus` enum and status field:\n   - Enum: `ACTIVE`, `CANCELLED`\n   - Add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` to Order data class\n   - New orders default to ACTIVE\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add query method:\n   - Add `fun findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments for an order\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Add cancel endpoint and logic:\n   - New method `cancel(@PathVariable orderId: String): ResponseEntity<Order>`\n   - Validates order exists (throw 404 if not)\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it (idempotent success)\n   - If any shipment for this order is CONFIRMED, throw 409 ConflictException without mutating\n   - If order is ACTIVE and no CONFIRMED shipments, transition to CANCELLED and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   - Return the updated order with 200 OK\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add order status check:\n   - Before creating shipment, check if order exists and has ACTIVE status\n   - If order doesn't exist, current behavior (let it proceed - ticket says \"keeps its current behaviour\")\n   - If order exists but is CANCELLED, throw 409 ConflictException with error code `ORDER_CANCELLED`\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Test: Cancel ACTIVE order transitions it to CANCELLED and updates CREATED shipments\n   - Test: Cancel ACTIVE order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with unchanged state\n   - Test: Cancel already CANCELLED order succeeds and returns order (idempotent)\n   - Test: Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n   - Test: Creating shipment on CANCELLED order returns 409\n   - Test: Each test verifies state through separate GET requests per testing-and-verification skill\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could put cancel logic in a separate OrderService class for better separation of concerns. Rejected because no service layer exists in this codebase; following existing patterns keeps changes minimal and maintains consistency with the baseline architecture.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with no CONFIRMED shipments\n- Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → found\n- Check: ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) → no CONFIRMED\n- Write: OrderRepository.save(order.copy(status=CANCELLED))\n- Write: ShipmentRepository.save for each CREATED shipment (update to CANCELLED)\n- Return: Order with status=CANCELLED, 200 OK\n\nCase 2: Cancel ACTIVE order with CONFIRMED shipment\n- Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → found\n- Check: ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) → found CONFIRMED\n- Throw: ConflictException(\"Cannot cancel order with confirmed shipments\")\n- Database: No changes\n- Return: 409 Conflict\n\nCase 3: Cancel already CANCELLED order\n- Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → found\n- Check: Order.status = CANCELLED\n- Return: Order as-is, 200 OK (idempotent success)\n\nCase 4: Cancel non-existent order\n- Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → null\n- Throw: ResourceNotFoundException\n- Return: 404 Not Found\n\nCase 5: Create shipment on CANCELLED order\n- Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → found\n- Check: Order.status = CANCELLED\n- Throw: ConflictException(\"Cannot create shipment for cancelled order\")\n- Return: 409 Conflict\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancelActiveOrderSucceeds()` - Creates order and CREATED shipment, cancels order, verifies order is CANCELLED through GET, verifies shipment is CANCELLED through GET\n2. `cancelOrderWithConfirmedShipmentReturns409()` - Creates order and CONFIRMED shipment, attempts cancel, verifies 409 response with error code, verifies order still ACTIVE through GET, verifies shipment still CONFIRMED through GET\n3. `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderSucceeds()` - Creates order, cancels it, cancels again, verifies second cancel succeeds with same result, verifies through GET\n4. `cancelNonExistentOrderReturns404()` - Attempts cancel on non-existent order, verifies 404 with error code\n5. `createShipmentOnCancelledOrderReturns409()` - Creates order, cancels it, attempts to create shipment, verifies 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED error code, verifies no shipment created\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":21898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1390},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fbe1112-45d2-46b9-9b0a-b993cb0189ba","uuid":"e8df2e2c-18a4-4973-bb8c-186382c3d589","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:34:15.150Z","request_id":"req_011CetRbeQNWoYHW19mWgdgv"}
